               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your patient, a 53-year-old female, who presented on 24/05/1993 with acute right lower quadrant abdominal pain, nausea, and low-grade fever, clinically consistent with acute appendicitis. Diagnostic workup including blood tests, physical examination, and abdominal ultrasound confirmed the diagnosis. The patient underwent a laparoscopic appendectomy without intraoperative complications. Postoperatively, she received intravenous fluids, analgesic medication, and wound care. Vital signs remained stable throughout her stay. She was mobilised early with physiotherapy support and discharged home on 27/05/1993 in good general condition. Please ensure follow-up wound inspection in approximately one week. Should any signs of surgical site infection or complications arise, early reassessment is recommended. Kind regards.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
